- **4xe plug-in hybrid** has a raised rear floor — needs 4xe-specific rear liners.
- **Drain plugs**: JL floors have drain plugs; liners with drain cut-outs are a nice-to-have.
- **Retention hooks**: factory driver-side hooks must line up — a mat without hook holes will slide under the pedals. All picks here are cut for the factory posts.
- **Stacking**: never lay a liner on top of the carpet mat. Remove the factory mat first.$g$, $f$[{"q": "TPE liners or rubber mats?", "a": "TPE liners (raised edges, laser-measured) hold water and snow and look OEM; rubber mats are cheaper, heavier and grip better but cover less of the footwell."}, {"q": "Do I need the 2nd-row piece?", "a": "Yes if anyone rides back there — mud collects on the rear floor first. Most sets here include 1st + 2nd row; 3rd-row and cargo liners are usually separate."}]$f$::jsonb, $v$**Budget:** a molded rubber set listed for your layout. **Best overall:** TPE laser-fit liners, 1st + 2nd row. **Premium:** maximum-coverage liners that run up the door sills.$v$, 'draft', CURRENT_DATE
FROM vehicles v JOIN makes m ON m.id=v.make_id JOIN categories c ON c.slug='floor-mats'
WHERE m.slug='jeep' AND v.model_slug='wrangler' AND v.gen_slug='2018-present'
ON CONFLICT (vehicle_id, category_id) DO UPDATE SET title=EXCLUDED.title, meta_desc=EXCLUDED.meta_desc, intro_md=EXCLUDED.intro_md,
  gotchas_md=EXCLUDED.gotchas_md, faq=EXCLUDED.faq, verdict_md=EXCLUDED.verdict_md, verified_at=EXCLUDED.verified_at, updated_at=now();

